1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,940
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:09,540
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,740
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,820
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:18,300
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,580
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,820
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,860
(Wang Churan)

9
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:30,300
=Natural High S4=

10
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,240
Our next mission

11
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,960
is called AI Q&A.

12
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:40,840
(AI Q&A)
We'll split into two teams of four.

13
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,560
Each team will take turns

14
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:43,920
as the presenting and guessing teams.

15
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:45,480
(AI Q&A: Presenting team)
The presenting team will receive

16
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:46,360
an AI-generated response

17
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:46,920
to a scenario.

18
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,440
The team must choose

19
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,520
one member

20
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:52,400
to deliver the AI's response.

21
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,040
The other three members

22
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,400
must improvise their own responses

23
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,400
to the same scenario,

24
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,600
imitating the AI's style

25
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,800
to cover for their teammate.

26
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,320
The presenting team can choose

27
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,640
any member of the guessing team
to partner with.

28
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,400
(AI Q&A: Guessing team)
The guessing team must watch

29
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,640
and identify which member

30
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,600
gave the AI-generated response.

31
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,720
Let's play a few bonus rounds.

32
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:14,960
(Guessing team, presenting team)

33
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,640
(Scenario:)
Your wounded nemesis is at your mercy.

34
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,600
You say something that breaks him.

35
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,320
(Flashbacks)
If you get too skinny, you won't look like me.

36
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:27,040
I'm burning up inside.

37
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,100
(It's time)

38
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,540
(What's in store for me?)

39
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,120
Do you need to see the card?
Guess not.

40
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:41,480
No need, right?

41
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,360
I'm not using AI anymore.

42
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:43,080
You don't need to see it, right?

43
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,420
(I'm better than AI anyway)
I'll come up with something myself.

44
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:46,780
(This one's aimed at me)

45
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,600
We can rule out Chengcheng.

46
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,360
The three of us have discussed it.

47
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,740
(AI response: I won't kill you.
I'll make you watch me win.)

48
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:00,520
Who'll say it?

49
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:00,920
I'll do it.

50
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,180
(Wang Churan performs the AI response)
You say it. Okay.

51
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:06,980
(AI performance: Wang Churan)

52
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,280
Do I have blood in my eyes?

53
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:10,520
He's out for blood.

54
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,800
Let's save Chengcheng for last.

55
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,200
Actually, Chengcheng should go first.

56
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,200
I've come up with an improvised rap.

57
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,020
(Emotion fuels creativity)

58
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,440
He goes last?

59
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:23,560
I'll go first.

60
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,260
(The weakest defense strikes again)

61
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,240
I'll go first, then.

62
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,360
I'll go easy on you, okay?

63
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:30,880
Okay.

64
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,040
Jingyu.

65
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,000
How am I supposed to end up
at her mercy?

66
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,040
Just lie on the floor.

67
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:45,540
(That loud?)

68
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:46,430
Oh my God.

69
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:49,900
(I heard that loud and clear)

70
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,120
That was so loud. What a crack.

71
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:56,660
(Loosening up)

72
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,020
(Getting into character)

73
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:05,580
(Waiting for the cue)

74
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:07,500
I won't "kill" you.

75
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,580
(Scenario:
Your wounded nemesis is at your mercy)

76
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,560
(You say something that breaks him)

77
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,560
I want you to watch me win.

78
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,480
I want you to watch me win.

79
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,560
You need to act like it broke you.

80
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,260
(Signaling him to play along)

81
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:18,780
(Oh, now I get it)

82
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,680
You have to act like it broke you.

83
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:25,120
Churan really wants Huang Jingyu

84
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,480
to act out the whole scenario.

85
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:28,820
Ah!

86
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,880
I don't want this leg either.

87
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,280
That really breaks you.

88
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,160
I'll go with Hu.

89
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:43,000
But he didn't necessarily injure me,
right?

90
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,360
I could've gotten hurt on my own

91
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,280
and then fallen into his hands.

92
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,440
(Determined to save face)

93
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:48,920
You can tell how competitive he is, huh?

94
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,440
You think he's not worthy
of hurting you, huh?

95
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,840
No, if he'd seriously injured me,

96
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:55,640
he wouldn't need to say a word.

97
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,000
He could just "kill" me.

98
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,400
(Right?)
You've got it right.

99
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,800
Come on, Hu. Let's start.

100
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,200
What rotten luck.

101
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:10,880
To think I'd end up in your hands.

102
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,120
Just finish me off.

103
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,000
You?

104
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,520
You think you're worthy
of falling into my hands?

105
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,180
(Why does that sound familiar?)

106
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:25,240
"You think he's not worthy
of hurting you, huh?"

107
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,880
Think you're worthy?

108
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,100
(He learns fast)

109
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,760
Finish yourself off.

110
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:41,520
Think you're worthy?

111
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:42,920
If that's an AI response,

112
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,300
I'll eat that card.

113
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,200
(A line tailored just for him)

114
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,040
How could AI pick up on your words?

115
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,660
(Just a fast learner)

116
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:50,800
Teng, you're up.

117
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,160
What are you doing?

118
00:04:59,160 --> 00:04:59,840
Um...

119
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,560
What's that for?

120
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:03,380
(Going by the script)

121
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,840
I'm taking you to the hospital now.

122
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:08,180
(That gentle?)

123
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:09,600
Once you're healed,

124
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,240
we'll do it all over again.

125
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,560
Just "kill" me!

126
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,080
He's still plotting something.

127
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,760
Chengcheng, got your move ready?

128
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:28,820
(Of course)

129
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:29,400
(Go easy on me, Chengcheng)

130
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,640
Can we air this?

131
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,720
As if Chengcheng cares if it airs.

132
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:34,880
He'll have his fun first.

133
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,720
This is already the nice version.

134
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,620
(Just thinking about it makes me laugh)

135
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,280
Lie down properly.

136
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:43,640
Face this way.

137
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,420
(Collapsing weakly)

138
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,360
(Keeping a low profile)
Yeah, face this way.

139
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,680
No, lie like this.

140
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,120
The lighting's better here.

141
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,820
(Better lighting for the shot)

142
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,400
You care about me that much?

143
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,480
(He does care about me)

144
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,080
You need to roast him until he cries.

145
00:05:57,660 --> 00:05:59,020
(Seriously?)

146
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:05,700
(Gathering to watch)

147
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,320
I won't "kill" you.

148
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,400
Because whether you're in this world

149
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,000
or not makes no difference.

150
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,140
(Sorry, Bai)

151
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:25,860
(Drowning on dry land)

152
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,420
(Rushing to the rescue)

153
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,660
(Here I come)

154
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:40,340
(Emotionally broken)

155
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:41,960
Did that break you?

156
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,580
(Hearing his heart shatter)

157
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,000
No one was even trying

158
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,320
to sound like AI.

159
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:51,840
Exactly.

160
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,600
They just wanted to have fun.

161
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:55,400
That felt great.

162
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:56,620
(Feeling much better)

163
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:57,800
Wang Churan.

164
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,100
(Guessed it already?)

165
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,200
Because AI responses

166
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,120
aren't usually that harsh.

167
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:03,960
Don't you think?

168
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:05,980
(I get a little flustered
under pressure)

169
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,720
Wait, I forgot what Churan said.

170
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,360
Same here.

171
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,140
(It's not harsh enough)

172
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,000
So I said it doesn't sound harsh.

173
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
I was saying,

174
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,720
I won't "kill" you.
I want you to watch me win.

175
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,440
Sounds like AI.

176
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,440
I'd say Wang Churan.

177
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,080
(Final choice: Wang Churan)
Wang Churan.

178
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,040
Congratulations.

179
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,200
Got it on the first try.

180
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,260
(Wang Churan: Correct)

181
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:27,940
(Sometimes spotting AI is that easy)

182
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:33,920
(Presenting team, guessing team)
A college classmate confesses to you.

183
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:36,920
(Scenario:)
Politely reject them in one sentence.

184
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,520
You've got the wrong person.

185
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:39,620
(Problem solved)

186
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,500
(Scenario:
A college classmate confesses to you.)

187
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:41,380
(You politely reject them
in one sentence.)

188
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:43,260
(Reading the prompt card)

189
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:46,100
(AI response:
I'm flattered you feel that way.)

190
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,380
(But I'm not ready to walk
the path of love with you.)

191
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,860
(Come discuss it privately)

192
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,760
Bai, you take this one.

193
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:56,460
(Bai Jingting performs the AI response)

194
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,520
That works, right?

195
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,680
Try inverting the sentence.

196
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,180
(Curious to see)

197
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,680
How would that sound?

198
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,960
Like you, I.

199
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:05,620
(Like you, I do.)

200
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:07,180
(Is that right?)

201
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,520
Really like you, I do.

202
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,940
Like you, I do.

203
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:11,720
Like you, I do.

204
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,520
I like you.

205
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,260
(Another Shandong phrase learned)

206
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:18,640
You can all choose Churan
as your partner.

207
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,740
(Four rejections coming her way)

208
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:24,240
I've never confessed before.
Let me think.

209
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:26,980
(AI performance: Bai Jingting)

210
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,780
(Scenario:
A college classmate confesses to you.)

211
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:30,700
(Politely reject them in one sentence.)

212
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:34,320
What's wrong, Churan?

213
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:37,520
Um...

214
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:40,840
Um...

215
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,240
Um...

216
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,180
(About to start throat singing)

217
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,360
Um...

218
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,800
Really like you, I do.

219
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:49,340
(Shandong girl mode activated)

220
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,220
(Trying not to laugh)

221
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,600
I really like you.

222
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:54,740
Oh, wow.

223
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,160
What do you think of me?

224
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,360
You're wonderful.

225
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,640
How could such good fortune

226
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:07,300
(Don't say that)
ever come my way?

227
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:08,780
(How poetic)

228
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,600
I think you deserve someone better.

229
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:14,960
That was really tactful.

230
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:16,780
(Is that how Teng talks?)

231
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,080
That was really tactful.

232
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,420
(Let's do something less tactful)

233
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:26,760
He's using the AI response.

234
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,720
Sounds like it.

235
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,120
Definitely.

236
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,380
(A little suspicious)

237
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,240
Keep going.

238
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:38,600
Um...

239
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:42,400
I think you're really handsome.

240
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:43,540
(Shandong girl is back)

241
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,120
What do you think of me?

242
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:46,100
(That charm is contagious)

243
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:50,760
What did you just say to me?

244
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,760
Shandong dialect is so fun.

245
00:09:57,980 --> 00:10:00,100
(Can't get enough of Shandong dialect)

246
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:03,160
(Picked it up in no time)
I think you're really handsome.

247
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,560
What do you think of me?

248
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,640
What do you think of me?

249
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:09,300
(Back to the point)

250
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:11,520
I'm really happy you like me.

251
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:12,480
You're a great person as well.

252
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,600
But for now, I think...

253
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,900
(Such formal wording)

254
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:15,880
We still have no way

255
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,280
to walk down the path of love together.

256
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:21,720
Have you been a domineering CEO
since your school days?

257
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:22,900
A "top student".
[*Chinese: Xue Ba]

258
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:23,780
(A "domineering" CEO during "student" days)
[*Xue: short for student, Ba: domineering]

259
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,040
A top student.

260
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,520
"Domineering" CEO during
"student" days. A "top student".

261
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,800
That's one way to interpret it.

262
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,580
(A brand-new definition)

263
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,820
(You're welcome to use it)

264
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:37,960
Come on, Bai.

265
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:39,220
(Go)

266
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,320
Let's hear those compliments.

267
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,860
(Ready for some praise)

268
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:56,600
Tired yet?

269
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,520
I've liked you for ages.

270
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:17,280
(Back to Shandong dialect in a flash)
I'm honored you like me.

271
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:19,000
But when it comes to love,

272
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,240
I can't walk that path
with you just yet.

273
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:24,300
(Give that back)

274
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,600
She took the water back as well.

275
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,240
Right.

276
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:29,000
She wants love without giving anything.

277
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,160
Cut your losses early.

278
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:33,520
That sounds like AI as well.

279
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,800
Just like the last one.

280
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,120
But I think it's Teng.

281
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,440
Teng wouldn't say something like that.

282
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:40,220
(The prime suspect)

283
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:41,000
Come on.

284
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:48,640
Doing homework?

285
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:53,940
(Want me to hold them?)

286
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,180
(Oh, okay)

287
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,760
Do you really not wanna see me?

288
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,200
What's up?

289
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,120
I've actually liked you for a long time.

290
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:08,760
Thanks.

291
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,120
And?

292
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:16,780
(Is this the art of conversation?)

293
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,080
So tactful.

294
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,310
Oh my God.

295
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,760
He wanted to hear
a few more compliments.

296
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:24,280
But he didn't get any.

297
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,080
Got it. I appreciate your feelings.

298
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,520
I'd rather focus on school.

299
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,040
It's over?

300
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,360
I mean, let's end this.

301
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:39,100
(Just end this nonsense already)

302
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,040
Take a guess.

303
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,520
I kinda forgot.

304
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:47,600
You listen more clearly

305
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,560
when you're not presenting.

306
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,040
Hu's definitely not AI.

307
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:51,840
(Hu is the first to be ruled out)
Hu's not AI.

308
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:52,480
Definitely not AI.

309
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,340
(Hu is watching)

310
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:55,640
What'd you say again, Teng?

311
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,840
Something about deserving better?

312
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:58,520
He said something about being lucky.

313
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,840
How could such good fortune
ever come my way?

314
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,520
But I think you deserve better.

315
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:05,080
That sounds like Teng.

316
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,080
That's nothing
like what Teng usually says.

317
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:07,600
I'm telling you.

318
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,440
(A brother knows best)
He'd never even think of that.

319
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,940
(Keep thinking that way)

320
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:14,700
(Rooting for you)

321
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,280
You're all in for a big surprise.

322
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:21,640
I think Jingyu kinda fits too.

323
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,960
That's just Jingyu being Jingyu.

324
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,900
(Quite the reputation)

325
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,480
That doesn't sound like

326
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:29,720
a compliment.

327
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:34,640
I'll go with you.

328
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,200
I'll go with you guys.

329
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:35,680
You pick.

330
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:37,880
Whoever you say.

331
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:38,600
Whoever I say?

332
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,640
Then Teng.

333
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,240
Okay.

334
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:41,400
You sure? Final answer?

335
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:42,600
Final.

336
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:44,040
Teng.

337
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,860
(Final pick: Shen Teng)
Lin has made his choice.

338
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:47,120
Did he get it right?

339
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:53,400
Congratulations.

340
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,600
You're wrong.

341
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,340
(Shen Teng: Wrong)

342
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,760
See? I told you it sounded like Jingyu.

343
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,280
I told you it sounded like Jingyu.

344
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:05,400
You pick up bad habits fast.

345
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,280
Of these four responses,

346
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,120
Teng's was the most tactful.

347
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:13,760
You're right about that.

348
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:14,380
(Bro approves)

349
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,440
So that means AI

350
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,180
(Teng's reasoning)
still has room to improve.

351
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,000
Right?

352
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:20,360
Right?

353
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,640
I'm ahead of the algorithm.

354
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:25,500
(Way ahead)

355
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,880
He had plenty
of practice when he was young.

356
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:31,240
So how many people
have you rejected with that line?

357
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:33,920
Bing, take a guess.

358
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:37,120
I actually wanted to pick Jingyu,

359
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,200
but I got a little scared.

360
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:39,800
Scared?

361
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,200
Scared it wasn't AI?

362
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,520
Afraid you'd ruin my whole image?

363
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:46,320
Just like that.

364
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:50,880
Churan, pick another.

365
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:51,960
You choose.

366
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:58,200
Now this guy's looking suspicious.

367
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,240
Why'd he go stand over there?

368
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:03,240
Just getting some sun.

369
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:04,720
(Getting some vitamin D)

370
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,800
I'd rather focus on school.

371
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:07,520
Can't be him.

372
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:09,560
(Stares)

373
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:10,400
Then Jingyu.

374
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,180
(Final pick: Huang Jingyu)
Jingyu.

375
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:14,880
Congrats, Churan.

376
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:16,480
(I got it. Yay)

377
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,020
You're wrong.

378
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:18,180
(Wait, I'm wrong?)

379
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:19,820
(Huang Jingyu: Wrong)

380
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,220
(Think harder)

381
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:24,560
Pick another.

382
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:25,960
(Stirring things up)
There's only one left. Hurry.

383
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,040
I told you Hu looked suspicious

384
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:28,800
in that corner.

385
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:29,760
Hu?

386
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:32,920
Okay, I'll pick Hu.

387
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:33,440
(I'll vote for him)

388
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:33,920
Congrats.

389
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:35,120
Wrong.

390
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:37,780
(Hu Xianxu: Wrong)

391
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,440
This spot really brings me luck.

392
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,240
My lucky spot.

393
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:44,080
See? Told you.

394
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:46,720
I'm not ready to walk
the path of love with you.

395
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:48,700
(Successfully stayed hidden)

396
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,160
Even if you get all three guesses wrong,

397
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,400
you'll just think

398
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:54,680
they act well.

399
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:55,440
You're not mad.

400
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:58,120
But Werewolf, you get mad
when you get it wrong.

401
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:00,920
So you just laugh
like an idiot when you're mad?

402
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:02,520
I've learned to take it in stride.

403
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:03,420
(The ultimate patience test)

404
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:05,640
(Guessing team, presenting team)
You submit a proposal to your boss.

405
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,360
(Scenario:)
What could your boss say

406
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:10,280
that would make you instantly lose it?

407
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,880
You used AI again, didn't you?

408
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:13,400
Even AI could do this job.

409
00:16:15,540 --> 00:16:18,820
(AI's response:
This proposal's nothing special)

410
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:22,140
(You wrote it,
so I wasn't expecting much anyway)

411
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:22,880
I think

412
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,740
(Discussing strategy)
it doesn't matter who's AI.

413
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,880
We should basically say the same thing.

414
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,000
(Confusing them with similar responses)

415
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:28,880
That'll make it harder to guess.

416
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:30,640
Makes sense.

417
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:31,600
(Strategy approved)

418
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:33,640
Then let's pick someone to play AI.

419
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,200
You be AI.

420
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:35,920
(Fan Chengcheng plays AI)
I'm AI?

421
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:36,480
You're AI.

422
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:37,680
We're ready.

423
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:38,800
Let's go.

424
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:39,960
(AI performance: Fan Chengcheng)

425
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:40,360
Lin.

426
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:43,580
(Here we go)

427
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:44,800
Who do you wanna roast, Lin?

428
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:46,800
Mr. Huang.

429
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:47,560
Me?

430
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,620
(Guess I'm the target)

431
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:51,500
(In position and ready to roast)

432
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:52,260
(Scenario: You submit
a proposal to your boss)

433
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:53,100
(What could your boss
say to make you lose it?)

434
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,040
Mr. Lin,

435
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,280
here's the proposal you wanted.

436
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,800
I rushed to finish it.
Please take a look.

437
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,320
This proposal's no good either.

438
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:06,440
You're just not cut out for this.

439
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:11,820
(Is that supposed to make him furious?)

440
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,920
I didn't even flinch.

441
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:15,600
(That barely hurt)

442
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:16,800
He's still a pretty gentle boss.

443
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:18,680
You're still playing that foreign CEO
with the steering wheel on the right.

444
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,740
(The overseas CEO makes a comeback)

445
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:23,880
His size kinda makes me

446
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,240
nervous.

447
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,560
With an employee like that,

448
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,240
even the boss
wouldn't dare push his luck.

449
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:33,160
Bing.

450
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:34,880
Alright.

451
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:35,520
Okay.

452
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,300
(Bing steps up)

453
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,040
Roast me.

454
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:38,060
(Ready to go)
Come on, Bing.

455
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:41,880
Mr. Jia.

456
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:42,200
Mr. Jia,

457
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:43,960
I stayed up all night
revising this proposal.

458
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:44,440
Please take a look.

459
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,520
No need. Just keep it.

460
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,720
Three years and you haven't improved.

461
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:59,080
(That's how you see my last three years?)
Three years and you haven't improved.

462
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:00,240
Three years?

463
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:01,280
Three years?

464
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,320
That one really stings.

465
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:04,740
(Can't take it anymore)

466
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:05,960
I'm absolutely furious.

467
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,680
Rumble!

468
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,080
Rumble!

469
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:09,820
(DIY thunderstorm)

470
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,320
Rumble?

471
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,100
(You're hilarious, Hu)

472
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:14,000
Okay.

473
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,180
(Let's go)

474
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,320
Who?

475
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:18,640
You pick.

476
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,220
(Choose your presenting partner)

477
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:20,960
Old man.

478
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:22,780
(It was meant to be)

479
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,360
Mr. Fan, I worked all night
on this proposal.

480
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:28,880
Take a look.

481
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,480
Please review it.

482
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,600
This proposal's nothing special.

483
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:34,760
You wrote it,

484
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:35,560
so I wasn't expecting much.

485
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,980
(Nobody believed in him from the start)

486
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:46,920
Mr. Fan is such a...

487
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,580
(Secret)

488
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:49,260
(Says it and runs)

489
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:53,600
Ms. Wang,

490
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,600
I stayed up all night
writing this proposal.

491
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:56,880
Leave it there.

492
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,120
No point even looking at it.

493
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,200
Don't waste my time again.

494
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:00,780
(Won't even look)

495
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:04,620
(Worked all night,
and she won't even glance at it)

496
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:07,460
(I threw it, so I'll pick it up)

497
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,160
Those were all pretty harsh.

498
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,420
(Still stuck in character)
It's okay, young man.

499
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:14,240
Rumble!

500
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,540
(Providing sound effects for Bai)

501
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,440
They all seem to have the same idea.

502
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,920
All four basically said the same thing.

503
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:19,680
Same message.

504
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,760
Just worded differently.

505
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,920
That makes it hard to guess.

506
00:19:22,380 --> 00:19:23,460
(Exactly what Bing wanted)

507
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:27,280
Their answers are 60% alike.

508
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:28,920
Just leave it there.

509
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,120
No need to look at it.

510
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:31,920
Anyway, you...

511
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,160
Only the last few words are different.

512
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,240
No way.

513
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,720
I need to see your prompt.

514
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:37,200
(Trying to peek at our cards?)

515
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,040
But then you'd...

516
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,120
You'd know the answer.

517
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:44,540
(When things get awkward, just laugh)

518
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,160
You're not even trying to hide it?

519
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,920
The two brain-fog buddies
are finally together.

520
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:51,700
(New brain-fog buddy)

521
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:54,400
Did the same guy hit both of us
on the head?

522
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,640
You were just gonna go over and look,

523
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:57,160
and then pick someone?

524
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,520
Hu, stay away.
Your stupidity's contagious.

525
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:04,840
What do you think, Churan?

526
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,160
Hold on.

527
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:08,760
Let me look again.

528
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:10,280
(Putting on an act)
Let's think.

529
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:10,760
Right.

530
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:13,320
I don't even remember what I said.

531
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:15,100
(Pretending to think)

532
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,920
Bing mentioned three years.

533
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:18,640
Something with that kind of backstory

534
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,400
doesn't really sound AI-generated.

535
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,400
You sure know AI well.

536
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,480
Or maybe Bing's answer
was AI-generated.

537
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,040
The other three made up similar answers,

538
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:31,880
but Bing gave a specific time frame.

539
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:34,360
Like, you haven't
improved in three years.

540
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:39,240
Wait, you weren't actually saying I
haven't improved in three years, right?

541
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:40,900
(An unexpected interpretation)

542
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:43,720
Jingyu.

543
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:47,400
What do you think?

544
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:48,940
(What's your answer?)

545
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:55,460
(Waiting for his verdict)

546
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,480
I can't tell.

547
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,080
(Intuition unavailable)

548
00:20:58,080 --> 00:20:59,880
He's learned his lesson.
He can't tell who.

549
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,000
Now we don't even have a lead.

550
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:03,080
(Can't rule anyone out now)

551
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:04,560
You've gotta give us something.

552
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,200
I'll rule one out first.

553
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:07,700
(Deep in thought)

554
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,080
I don't think it's Bing.

555
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:14,020
(Trusting his gut)

556
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:17,660
(Can't keep a straight face)

557
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:20,200
The moment you ruled out Bing,

558
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,880
Wang Churan almost burst out laughing.

559
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,760
I'm just in a good mood today.

560
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:29,740
(An unexpected explanation, finally)

561
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:32,280
She's terrifying!

562
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,040
She just said out of nowhere,

563
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:36,120
"I'm just in a good mood today."

564
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:39,260
(A perfect impression)

565
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,120
But Chengcheng's answer

566
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,680
was actually really similar to Yunrui's.

567
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,980
(This proposal's
nothing special..., This proposal...)

568
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:52,400
(Chengcheng, Yunrui)

569
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:52,960
Let's go with Chengcheng.

570
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:53,580
(Trusting his gut)

571
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,080
Agreed?

572
00:21:56,180 --> 00:21:57,260
(Guys, say something)

573
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,400
I'm the one making
all the decisions anyway!

574
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:00,560
Sound good?

575
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:01,600
Let's lock it in.

576
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,780
(Final pick: Fan Chengcheng)

577
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:06,160
Congratulations.

578
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,320
Hu got it on the first try.

579
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:09,900
(Fan Chengcheng: Correct)

580
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,300
(They caught me)

581
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:15,000
See? Told you.

582
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:17,020
(Never misses a chance
to tease his little bro)

583
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:18,680
Why are you so annoying?

584
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,880
I don't think Bing,

585
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:23,400
Lin, or Churan were AI.

586
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:25,620
(Everyone's an expert after the fact)
You guys guess.

587
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:26,480
Now that you mention it...

588
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:27,560
Who?

589
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:28,640
Chengcheng?

590
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:29,200
Chengcheng.

591
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:30,100
(Anyu told me)

592
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:34,400
So Bing was just
straight-up insulting me.

593
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:36,380
(Back to that again)

594
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:38,200
I'll keep working hard, Bing.

595
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,940
(I'm crying)
It's okay.

596
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:44,300
(Just kidding)

597
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:47,080
So when you're training your AI,

598
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:48,160
you've gotta treat it well.

599
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:49,240
(What's that supposed to mean?)

600
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,880
Seriously, be nice to it.

601
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,880
Every time I use AI,

602
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:52,840
I always say thank you.

603
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:53,540
(Such good manners)

604
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:55,760
What does the AI say?

605
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,320
It ignores me.

606
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:00,080
Bing's got it all figured out.

607
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:02,000
When AI eventually takes over,

608
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,760
he'll say, I was always nice to you.

609
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:04,080
Exactly.

610
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:04,860
(Claiming the moral high ground with AI)

611
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:05,920
It's karma.
